{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# A2A \u2014 The Agent-to-Agent Protocol Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements an A2A-minimal server and client using `http.server` and JSON. The server:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- exposes `/.well-known/agent.json`,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- accepts `POST /tasks`,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- manages task state,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- returns artifacts on `GET /tasks/{id}`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The client:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- fetches the Agent Card,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- submits a task,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- polls until completion,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- reads the artifact."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The script starts the server in a background thread, then runs the client against it. You see the complete flow: discovery, submit, poll, artifact."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Run `code/main.py`. Confirm the client discovers the server and receives the correct artifact.\n2. Add a second skill to the server (e.g., \"summarize\"). Update the Agent Card. Write a client that picks the skill based on task type.\n3. Implement an SSE streaming endpoint: `/tasks/{id}/events` that emits state changes. What does the client need to do differently?\n4. Read the A2A spec (https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/specification/). Identify three things the spec mandates that this demo does not implement.\n5. Compare A2A (Agent Card discovery) to MCP (server-side capability listing via `listTools`). What is the tradeoff between self-describing agents and capability-probing?"
      ]
    }
  ],
